  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1141 PM CDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\nWednesday's rain chances will be highly contingent on how the \naforementioned upper level low comes across. The low may \npotentially come across the Southern Great Plains in such a way \nthat the central to southwestern parts of the Panhandles end up \ngetting dry slotted with the eastern and northern portions getting\nsome additional rounds of rain. The eastern parts of the \nPanhandles getting more rain on Wed/Wed night may only be the case\nif the low doesn't move off too fast and dry slots that area. \nThere will also be chances for wrap around moisture to add \nadditional rounds of light to moderate showers Thu and Thu night. \nFor now extra cloud cover is expected to keep afternoon \ntemperatures cooler in the 70s for the most part through the \nweekend. With Friday potentially having the coolest temps, \npotentially staying in the upper 60s. This will be thanks to the \narrival of a cold front Thursday. This cold front on Thursday may \nalso bring in some strong northerly winds behind it, and would not\nrule out potential headlines like a wind advisory.",
